  "changes": "initial namespace/dependency extraction from fixed PR head; host weight/state separation; ATOM IPC/compile runtime integration; exact-row target runner; lossless post-load V4 binder; real BF16 cache/metadata adapter; ordinary token entry and S1 engine lifecycle hooks; device dependency cache key expanded; deterministic radix winner compaction replaces atomic output-slot allocation without changing radix membership; BF16 KV NoPE round-trip is a compile-profile option and disabled for real BF16 cache; real non-fused shared Expert has an explicit BF16/block128 E8M0 profile, including independent pre-routed-quantization input and BF16 gate/activation boundaries; real routed down preserves each full-K route until weighted BF16 conversion, then BF16 routed sum/shared add; Opus routed UG retains FP32 prequant activation; real main/index compressor projections have a BF16 full-K epilogue before gate/ring publication; real attention uses FP8/block128 E8M0 inputs and BF16 projection outputs, fused FP32 q-norm requantization, FP32 sparse split partials and inverse-RoPE publication; real mHC normalization uses FP32 collapsed sqrsum with a BF16 numerator and HC4 pair-tree contraction, and gfx950 hidden7168 M1 reproduces the ordinary 256-thread/four-wave raw sqrsum reduction tree; main/index compressor pooling/norm/RoPE retain FP32 until cache/quant write, and real index query has no extra BF16 RoPE seam; existing observer plane records actual CSA BF16 weights-projection operands for fixed-input attribution; real CSA indexer Hadamard disabled to match ATOM; ONE layer grid and peer protocol retained; current real-model replay binaries are NOT the initial byte-exact performance-port binaries; standalone layer wrapper split from the serving runner into layer.py; production admission moved to ATOM-owned dispatch.py",
